,\\n2026-12-31,food,2,\\n2027-01-01,food,9,\\n2026-11-02,b,3,\\n2026-11-03,a,3,\\n\")\n    before = p.read_bytes()\n    cases = [[\"2026-12\"], [\"2026-11\"], [\"2026-13\"], [\"2026-00\"], [\"2026-9\"], [\"2026-09-15\"], [\"abc\"], [\"0000-01\"], [\"2026-W1\"], [\"\"], [\"２０２６-12\"], []]\n    for c in cases:\n        out, err = io.StringIO(), io.StringIO()\n        code = None\n        with redirect_stdout(out), redirect_stderr(err):\n            try:\n                code = main([\"--file\", str(p), \"month\", *c])\n            except SystemExit as e:\n                code = e.code\n        print(c, code, repr(out.getvalue()), repr(err.getvalue().strip().splitlines()[-1:] ))\n    print(\"unchanged\", p.read_bytes() == before)\n    out = io.StringIO()\n    with redirect_stdout(out):\n        main([\"--file\", str(Path(d) / \"missing.csv\"), \"month\", \"2026-12\"])\n    print(\"missing\", repr(out.getvalue()))\n"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"extra_usage_disabled","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":7,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I found no spec or CLAUDE.md violations, a few minor quality issues, and nothing out of scope. This was a review by reading the code only: the sandbox blocked my probe script, so none of the inputs below were actually run.\n\n## 1. Spec / CLAUDE.md violations\nNone. Requirement by requirement:\n- **R1, R2, ties:** `total_by_category` uses a stable sort on a dict that keeps first-appearance order, so equal totals stay in file order, as `summary` does. The total line comes from `monthly_total`, as the spec requires.\n- **R3:** with no argument, `default=None` is not passed through `type=`, so `date.today()` supplies the year and month (`cli.py:105-107`).\n- **R4:** `2026-13`, `2026-00`, `2026-9`, `2026-09-15`, `abc`, `0000-01` and full-width digits like `２０２６-12` are all rejected by the shape check or `fromisoformat`. Each raises `ArgumentTypeError` with the exact spec message, so the exit code is 2 and nothing goes to stdout.\n- **R5:** a missing file gives `[]` from `load_expenses`, and an empty file gives no rows, so the output is only `total 0.00`.\n- **R6:** the filter checks both year and month, so the Dec/Jan boundary case is correct.\n- **R7:** the command never calls `append_expense`.\n- **R8:** `expenses_in_month` raises `ValueError` for a month outside 1–12 (`report.py:37`).\n- **Module jobs:** filtering is in `report.py` and the CLI only formats. The README has its one usage line, and the new report function has a docstring that says how it rounds.\n\n## 2. Risks / code-quality issues (all low)\n1. **Help text shows `month [month]`, not `[YYYY-MM]`.** The positional has no `metavar`, so `month -h` and the usage line in error messages show `month [month]`, while the spec writes `month [YYYY-MM]`. Also, `args.month` holds a `(year, month)` tuple, which is easy to misread as an int. Fix: add `metavar=\"YYYY-MM\"`; a clearer `dest` is optional.\n2. **The month filter is written twice.** `expenses_in_month` and `monthly_total` use the same year-and-month condition. The spec requires both functions and forbids changing `monthly_total`, so this is accepted. It's still worth knowing that the two copies could drift apart later.\n3. **The validation condition is hard to read.** `year_month` packs five checks into one line (`cli.py:38`). It's correct, and the `isascii()` guard against non-ASCII digits is a good catch. Splitting it, or adding a comment that names what each check rejects, would make it easier to maintain. Building the `ArgumentTypeError` before the checks is harmless.\n\n## 3. Built but out of scope\nNone. The diff doesn't touch `add`, `list`, `summary`, `between`, `monthly_total`, `data/` or `docs/`, and adds no new dependencies.","ttft_ms":8932,"type":"result","duration_ms":85980,"uuid":"8fb11b63-8ad5-4807-bcca-f1823f11583f","ttft_stream_ms":8405,"time_to_request_ms":244,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":9,"system_prompt":34,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":6,"input_attachments":36,"input_hooks":4,"conversation_append":2,"transcript_persist":26,"tool_pool_refresh":8,"init_message":32,"init_frame_send":8,"engine_pickup":2,"loop_entry":9,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":6,"autocompact":3,"request_announcements":17,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":13,"message_normalization":4,"client_creation":3,"request_build":19},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":53,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":406,"time_to_request_major_faults":6357,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"deferred_tools_delta","slowest_producer_ms":15,"cpu_ms":94,"major_faults":1176,"setup_ms":2,"prompt_producers_ms":2,"ambient_start_ms":12,"ambient_wait_ms":14,"render_ms":4,"producers":40,"token_counts":0},"tool_schema_build_detail":{"betas_ms":1,"waits_ms":1,"placement_ms":3,"render_ms":7,"after_ms":1,"other_ms":0,"tools":14,"new_schemas":14},"message_normalization_detail":{"before_ms":0,"normalize_ms":3,"images_ms":0,"post_process_ms":1,"after_ms":0,"other_ms":0,"messages":13,"wire_messages":2},"request_build_detail":{"records_ms":1,"system_ms":1,"headers_ms":1,"cache_break_record_ms":2,"plans_ms":2,"retry_setup_ms":0,"sent_build_ms":3,"record_attempt_ms":9,"other_ms":0,"sent_build_safety_context_ms":0,"sent_build_cache_breakpoints_ms":0,"sent_build_surrogate_scan_ms":1},"first_content_frame_ms":8406,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":4373,"outputTokens":14,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.00044430000000000007,